## Actual Image Observations

The original PNG and the existing complete modern PNG were each viewed once:
two image views total, zero crops/reopens. The full modern square, rightmost and
bottommost branches, grid, axes and arrowheads were visible.

Both actual images visibly carry Roman I, II, III, IV curve labels. I/II are
the wider/narrower upward-opening solid curves; III/IV are the wider/narrower
downward-opening solid curves. No A/B labels were invented. The graph supplies
the readable points `(1,1)`, `(1,2)`, `(2,-1)`, `(1,-1)` respectively, not
printed coefficient answers. The source form therefore determines one `a`
for every curve without using its vertex.

